@startuml
title American Airlines Monthly Bidding Lifecycle & Daily Timelines

actor "Flight Attendant" as FA
participant "TBS / LRD Systems" as Phase1
participant "PBS Bidding Engine" as Phase2
participant "TTS / UBL / ROTA" as Phase3

== Phase 1: Training & Status Preference ==
FA -> Phase1 : Day 1 (12:00 CT): TBS opens for Training/CQ bids
FA -> Phase1 : Day 3 (12:00 CT): LRD opens for Lineholder/Reserve toggles
FA -> Phase1 : Day 6 (12:00 CT): TBS closes and locks preferences
Phase1 -> FA : Day 7 (12:00 CT): TBS awards visible & LRD closes

== Phase 2: Monthly Preferential Bidding ==
Phase1 -> Phase2 : Day 9 (12:00 CT): Prior-month schedule feed cutoff
FA -> Phase2 : Day 10 (12:00 CT): PBS monthly bidding window opens
FA -> Phase2 : Day 15 (12:00 CT): PBS monthly bidding window closes & locks
Phase2 -> FA : Day 18 (12:00 CT): PBS awards posted (Monthly schedules visible)

== Phase 3: Post-Award Workflows & Daily ROTA ==
Phase2 -> Phase3 : Day 19 (12:00 CT): Awards visible in operational schedule
FA -> Phase3 : Day 20 (06:00 CT): TTS & Reserve day-off workflows open
Phase3 -> FA : Day 21 (06:00 CT): First TTS batch processing results shown
FA -> Phase3 : Day 22 (06:00 CT): ETB opens for real-time trip trades
FA -> Phase3 : Day 27 (12:00 CT): Golden/Flex day designation cutoff

== Note: The Daily Live Engine (Days 20 - End of Month) ==
... The following system loops every single day ...
FA -> Phase3 : 04:00 - 14:45 HBT: Continuous next-day UBL auto-awards run
FA -> Phase3 : 15:00 HBT: ROTA Automated Run locks bids (Standby & RAP processing)
Phase3 -> FA : 15:01+ HBT: ROTD Live Assignment takes over for late trips
FA -> Phase3 : 22:30 HBT: Deadline to acknowledge assigned sequences/standbys
@enduml
